# Worker-specific environment for mecha-school-outbox-worker.service.
#
# NOT A SECRET. This file holds a credential PATH and nothing else. Never add a
# service-account JSON, a private key, a database URL, a token or any other
# secret value here — it is tracked in git.
#
# Why this file exists
# ────────────────────
# systemd.exec(5), EnvironmentFile=: "Settings from these files override
# settings made with Environment=." An Environment= line in the unit therefore
# cannot win against the shared /var/www/mecha-school/.env, which the web tier
# and this worker both load. When several EnvironmentFile= entries set the same
# variable, they are read in the order listed and the last one wins, so the
# unit lists this file AFTER the shared .env.
#
# The defect this closes
# ──────────────────────
# The shared .env carried GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=firebase-key.json.
# A relative path resolves against WorkingDirectory=/var/www/mecha-school, i.e.
# the deploy checkout, where a stale service-account key sat untracked. The
# worker loaded it, Firebase answered "invalid_grant: Invalid JWT Signature",
# and five delivery attempts died — while the web tier, pointed at the
# protected key, kept working.
#
# Installed path: /var/www/mecha-school/deploy/mecha-school-outbox-worker-environment
# Deployed by the normal checkout; no separate operator copy step is required.
#
# If the key ever moves, change it here and in the shared .env.

GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/etc/mecha-school/firebase-key.json
